      "n": 1,
      "signpost": "almost not",
      "definition": "almost not, or only just",
      "explanation": "**Scarcely** already has a negative meaning, so it is not used with **not** or **never**. It often goes with **any**, **anyone**, **ever**, and **can** or **could**, and usually comes before the main verb.",
