  "synonym_discrimination": {
    "words": [
      "scarcely-adv",
      "hardly-adv",
      "barely-adv"
    ],
    "note": "All three can mean *almost not*. **Hardly** is the everyday choice (*I hardly slept*). **Barely** stresses that something only just happened or was only just enough: *we barely had time*. **Scarcely** means the same as **hardly** in most uses but is less common in speech and more common in writing: *the town had scarcely changed*."
